    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Morton et al. (1956) noticed a useful feature of this model. Recall that for a balanced polymorphism maintained by overdominance, the equilibrium allele frequencies are $ q_i = t_i/(s_i + t_i) $ and $ p_i = s_i/(s_i + t_i) $. Substituting these into the previous expressions,",
